WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.734
-Welcome, everybody. Welcome to

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.634
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:03.601
Thank you for being here.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:04.300
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.534
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:06.767
It's going to be
a fun show tonight.

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:08.868
Let's get to some news, guys.

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:10.267
It was just announced that the

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:13.067
U.S. District Judge
Raymond Dearie

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:15.100
will serve as the special master

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.267
and review the 11,000 documents
seized from Mar-A-Lago.

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:20.467
Wow, what a nightmare.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:21.901
That's basically
like being forced to read

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:23.334
Apple's terms and conditions.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:26.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.367
Seriously, that's crazy.
11,000 documents?

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:29.667
I wouldn't even read
a text message

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.300
longer than two sentences.
I go, "No."

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:34.100
That's right,
Raymond Dearie has been chosen

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.334
to serve as "special master"

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:38.367
and to gain some insight
into his work ahead,

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:41.067
we have Judge Dearie
with us tonight.

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:42.200
Hello, Your Honor?

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.501
-Jimmy, could you give me
just a moment?

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:45.601
I need to take this call.

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:46.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:47.701
-Sure.
Go right ahead.

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:50.501
-So, what were you asking
about those documents?

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:52.100
-[ As Trump ] What if you
accidentally lost them?

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.367
-Can't do it.
-Burned them?

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:54.434
-No.
-Shredded them?

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:55.434
-No.
-Flushed them?

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:56.634
-No.
-Ate them?

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:57.834
-Unh-unh.
-Spilled bleach on them?

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:58.767
-No.
-Ketchup?

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.200
-No!
-Fed them to a goat?

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.400
-No.
-Donkey?

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.634
-Nope.
-What if you burned them?

00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:03.968
-You already asked that one.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:04.767
Still no.

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:05.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:06.367
-You're a loser.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:07.067
[ Click, dial tone ]

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.868
-Sorry there, Jimmy.
What were you asking?

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:12.200
-You seem like you have a lot
on your plate there, Your Honor.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.000
Judge Dearie,
ladies and gentlemen, with us.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.400
Thank you very much.
I'm sorry about that.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.167
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]
Busy.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.634
Meanwhile, in a new interview,
former President Trump said

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.901
that he can't imagine
being indicted,

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.267
but that, even if he were,

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:27.300
it wouldn't stop him
from running again.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.200
[ Laughter ]
-Oh!

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.767
[ Booing ]

00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:32.334
In other words, Trump has
no idea what indicted means.

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:34.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:35.901
That's right,
there's a good chance

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:37.033
Trump could be
the first candidate

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:38.968
whose campaign bus
is a police cruiser.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:40.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.934
Well, yeah, if you haven't
heard about this already,

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.367
everyone's still talking
about how

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:46.167
Florida Governor Ron DeSantis
sent two planes of migrants

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.501
to Martha's Vineyard.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:48.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:49.934
When you think about it,
what's more American

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.667
than randomly landing
in Massachusetts,

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.167
with no plan
for what comes next?

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.234
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:56.300
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.801
People are calling it
a political stunt

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:04.567
and, now,
things are getting petty.

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:07.200
In response to DeSantis,
the governor of Massachusetts

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.367
just sent 50 Wahlberg brothers
to Florida.

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:10.968
-Oh.
-Yeah, unbelievable.

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:14.334
Guys, I heard that,
due to supply chain issues,

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.701
major pharmacy chains
across the U.S.

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:20.167
are experiencing a shortage
of Adderall.

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:21.934
In response, one guy was like,
"It's not my fault.

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:23.534
I have to read
11,000 documents.

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:24.701
I mean, I --

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:25.400
How am I supposed to --"

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:27.334 --> 00:02:29.400
Hey, let's just lighten
things up real quick, okay?

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.667
Last night, President Biden was
at a gala

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.601
and he decided to sing
"Happy Birthday"

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:35.734
to a California congresswoman.

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:36.701
[ Laughter ]
Let's see how that went.

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:40.434
-♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:43.400
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:46.200
♪ Happy birthday, da da ♪

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.334
[ Laughter ]
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:50.734
-Oh! Oh.
-God love you, kiddo.

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.100
-Wow, that's amazing. Wow.
-Aww.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.000
-[ Faux sniffles ]

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.167
There's nothing more touching

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:58.534
than someone singing
"Happy Birthday"

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:00.267
and not remembering your name.

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:01.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:03.467
It's the one line you have
to remember!

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:05.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:09.601
That's the money of that song,
is the name.

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.300
We all know the lyrics.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.701
♪ Happy birthday, ya ya ba ♪

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:18.767
♪ Ah da ya ♪
Whatever. Yeah, I'm tired.

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:21.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.934
Safe to say Biden
won't be getting a job

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:24.734
at Applebee's anytime soon.

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:26.534
♪ Happy ♪
Who cares?

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:28.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:30.634
Well, hey, listen to this --
I read that the Senate

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:33.767
just confirmed their first ever
cyber ambassador,

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:35.067
who will be responsible
for dealing

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:37.868
with international
cybersecurity issues.

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:40.133
Cyber ambassador,
special master --

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:42.033
these guys sound
like rejected characters

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:43.300
who would work for Darth Vader.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.434
[ Laughter ]
It's like, "Sir, sir,

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:46.100
the cyber ambassador is here
to see you."

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.868
[ Inhales sharply, baritone ]
Send them to the special master.

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:50.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:52.968
Cyber ambassador?

00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:55.767
Cyber ambassador -- sounds like
the IT guy asked for a raise

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:58.000
and they were like, "Uh,
how about a fancy name, instead?

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.734
[ Laughter ]
You're the cyber ambassador.

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:02.133
Now, can we get
this printer working?

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:03.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:06.467
Some news from overseas --
the prime minister of Pakistan

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:08.234
met with Vladimir Putin
and it looked like

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:11.367
he was really struggling
with his translation headphones.

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:12.300
Take a look at this.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:15.534
[ Laughs ]

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:17.300
[ Camera shutter clicks ]

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:18.334
Uh-huh.

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:19.534
Ooh!

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:22.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:24.167
There you go.

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:25.200
Ooh.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.367
-[ Speaking foreign language ]

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.200
There you go.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.734
Hold on.

00:04:33.734 --> 00:04:35.000
-Can somebody help me?

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.033
-Yeah.
-Aww!

00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:38.501
-There you go.

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:39.801
There you go.

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:41.000
There we go.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.901
-[ Speaking foreign language ]

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:46.334
[ Camera shutter clicking ]

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:48.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:52.167
[ Sad trombone plays ]

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:54.467
That guy is the leader
of 220 million people.

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:56.300
I just want
to let you know that.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.634
And then he finally
got the headset in

00:04:57.634 --> 00:04:59.133
and his pants fell down.
-Oh, no!

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:01.767
[ Laughter ]
-Isn't that unbelievable?
That's unbelievable.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:05.467
Guys, this is fun -- tomorrow,
for the first time since 2019,

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:07.934
Oktoberfest kicks off in Munich.

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:08.634
-[Both] Yeah!

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:12.033
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:14.100
Yeah!

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:17.601
It's that classic time
for Oktoberfest --

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:18.534
September.

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:21.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:22.834
Tomorrow is Oktoberfest.

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:23.634
It begins in Munich.

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:24.701
Meanwhile, here in New York,

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:26.667
the UN General Assembly
is underway,

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:28.300
so we thought we'd introduce
a new segment called

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.901
World Leaders Are More Fun
with Oompah Music.

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:31.901
[ Laughter ]
Check it out.

00:05:31.901 --> 00:05:34.567
♪♪

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:37.701
♪♪
[ Clapping rhythmically ]

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:45.267
♪♪

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:47.601
Whoa!

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:48.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:49.601
♪♪

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:50.267
Hey.

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:52.434
♪ Hey, hoh, hup ♪

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:55.968
♪♪
[ Clapping continues ]

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:57.767
Hey.

00:05:57.767 --> 00:05:59.000
There you go.
Not bad.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.534
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:02.534 --> 00:06:03.567
Well, this is
very interesting --

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:05.567
I saw that a growing number
of men

00:06:05.567 --> 00:06:07.067
are getting an expensive surgery

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:11.067
that lengthens their legs,
so that they can be taller.

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:12.868
Higgins, would you ever
do something like that?

00:06:12.868 --> 00:06:15.300
-No, probably not.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.400
I mean, if the recovery time
was short

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:20.801
or I had a doctor I trusted,
maybe, but,

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:22.300
I feel pretty good about myself.
-Yeah, that's good. Yeah.

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:24.367
What about you, Tariq?

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:25.467
-Definitely not.

00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:27.467
[ Laughter ]
I don't know why some men

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:28.901
are insecure about their height.

00:06:28.901 --> 00:06:30.267
I've always been comfortable

00:06:30.267 --> 00:06:32.367
with the height
I've always been --

00:06:32.367 --> 00:06:33.400
7'1".

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:34.968
[ Laughter ]
How about you, Jimmy?

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:36.734
-No way.
I mean, even if there were

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:39.234
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]
no medical risks

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:43.801
to the procedure, I-I --

00:06:43.801 --> 00:06:45.601
I still wouldn't --
still wouldn't do it!

00:06:45.601 --> 00:06:46.968
Aaaah!
-Hold on, Jimmy!

00:06:46.968 --> 00:06:48.434
[ Thudding ]
Jimmy, no, no!

00:06:48.434 --> 00:06:50.634
[ Tranquil tune plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:53.400
♪♪

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:56.133
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:06:56.133 --> 00:06:58.100
-That was like a little play.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.267
[ Rimshot ]

00:06:59.267 --> 00:07:00.567
Oh!
-Ah!

00:07:00.567 --> 00:07:01.467
-[ As Jerry Lewis ]
Tony Award.

00:07:01.467 --> 00:07:03.067
[ Laughter ]
-And, finally,

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:07.133
France just unveiled a new
high-speed train coming to Paris

00:07:07.133 --> 00:07:10.634
that can reach a maximum speed
of nearly 220 miles per hour.

00:07:10.634 --> 00:07:12.334
[ Oohs ]
It's an amazing service.

00:07:12.334 --> 00:07:14.767
You get to work early
and you get free Botox.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:15.968
[ Laughter and applause ]
We have a great show, everybody.

